{"content":[{"c":["CITADEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A city’s stronghold, tower, or fortification of last resort where people sought safety during an attack. The citadel of Penuel was destroyed by Gideon after he captured two Midianite kings (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.17","r":"Judg.8.17","rawR":"Judg.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.17","value":"Judg.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:17"},"). The citadel of El-berith at Shechem was burned to the ground by Abimelech and his men (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.46-49","r":"Judg.9.46-49","rawR":"Judg.9.46-49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.46-49","value":"Judg.9.46-49"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:46-49"},"). Abimelech was killed shortly thereafter when a woman in the citadel at Thebez dropped a millstone on his head and crushed his skull (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.50-54","r":"Judg.9.50-54","rawR":"Judg.9.50-54","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.50-54","value":"Judg.9.50-54"}],"t":"ref","v":"50-54"},"). David conquered Jerusalem by capturing its citadel (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.7-9","r":"2Sam.5.7-9","rawR":"2Sam.5.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.7-9","value":"2Sam.5.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:7-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.5-8","r":"1Chr.11.5-8","rawR":"1Chr.11.5-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.5-8","value":"1Chr.11.5-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:5-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["During the Maccabees’ struggle for independence in the second century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", the citadel in Jerusalem often aided the party in power (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.1.29-33","r":"1Macc.1.29-33","rawR":"1Macc.1.29-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.1.29-33","value":"1Macc.1.29-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 1:29-33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.11.41-42","r":"1Macc.11.41-42","rawR":"1Macc.11.41-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.11.41-42","value":"1Macc.11.41-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:41-42"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.13.49-51","r":"1Macc.13.49-51","rawR":"1Macc.13.49-51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.13.49-51","value":"1Macc.13.49-51"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:49-51"},"). The Fortress of Antonia, the Jerusalem citadel in the day of Jesus, fell to the Romans in ",{"c":["AD"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," 70."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Citadel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.17","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.17","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.17"},{"anchorText":"9:46-49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.9.46-49","rawQueryValue":"Judg.9.46-49","sourceRefExact":"Judg.9.46-49"},{"anchorText":"50-54","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.9.50-54","rawQueryValue":"Judg.9.50-54","sourceRefExact":"Judg.9.50-54"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:7-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.7-9","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.7-9","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.7-9"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:5-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.5-8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.5-8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.5-8"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 1:29-33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.1.29-33","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.1.29-33","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.1.29-33"},{"anchorText":"11:41-42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.11.41-42","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.11.41-42","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.11.41-42"},{"anchorText":"13:49-51","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.13.49-51","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.13.49-51","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.13.49-51"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7f18d80671bcae82c03e5d9dcf8472997f61be6411140116accb928fb1ca9cd6","sourceItemName":"Citadel","sourceItemOrder":196,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Citadel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Citadel","title":"Citadel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}